# DTF tier manifest: repo-delete-reclaims-storage-job
#   artifact-keeper#4311: deleting a large repository behind a proxy with a
#   30 s route timeout answers 202 with a job, the job completes, and an
#   identical upload into another repository during the delete keeps its
#   object.
#   Profile-set: storage.s3 (MinIO; every repository shares one bucket, so
#   identical content in two repositories is one object) +
#   proxy.route-timeout (a reverse proxy that answers 504 when the backend
#   has not started its response within 30 s, published on TRIVY_PORT).
#
# THE GAPS
#   * DELETE /api/v1/repositories/{key} collected the repository's storage
#     keys and ran the database cascade inside the request. A repository of
#     10,000 artifacts behind a proxy with a 30 s timeout got 504 (or the
#     server's own request-timeout SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE).
#   * The purge after the delete removed every key judged unshared at
#     collection time, with no record and no second look. The same bytes
#     uploaded into another repository after the collection deduplicated
#     against the object the purge then deleted, so that repository's artifact
#     no longer downloaded. The fix journals each key and re-checks references
#     immediately before each delete.
#
# Gates:
#   (CONTROL, both images) seeding: 10,000 artifact rows in repository A
#   whose objects are in the bucket, plus the shared payload uploaded to A
#   through the API (its SHA-256 sorts last, so a key-ordered purge reaches
#   it last); a small DELETE through the proxy of an empty repository
#   succeeds.
#   (FIX) DELETE of A through the proxy answers 202 within the timeout with a
#   job id and Location; A's key stops resolving at once; the shared payload
#   uploaded to repository B right after the DELETE response commits; the job
#   reports completed through GET /api/v1/repository-deletions/{id} (via the
#   proxy) with completed_items = 10,001; A's objects are gone from the
#   bucket; B's artifact still downloads byte-identical.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle seeds and polls back to back.
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.11.5. Green: ak-backend:lane-w3a.
PROFILES="storage.s3 proxy.route-timeout"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
